WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.930
One day, an email comes
from Eichi in America!

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.230
The unexpected good news
brightens Mitsuki's spirits

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:09.460
and even helps her condition improve!

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:14.460
But then we find out that the email
was actually a fake, sent from Izumi!

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:18.760
Takuto! How do we tell Mitsuki the truth?

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:22.830
So, I wonder what's
going to happen today...

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:28.560
Got that?

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:29.800
Yes.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:10.930
<i>Eichi... The minute that</i>
<i>email from you came,</i>

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:13.230
<i>I got word of a new operation.</i>

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:17.660
<i>It's like you brought me happiness!</i>

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:22.730
Takuto...

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:27.330
What are we going to do?
About Eichi's email being a fake.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:28.530
Should we tell her?

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:34.000
Yes, Ms. Oshige?

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:36.530
Yes...

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:38.330
What?

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:41.660
I've been nominated for
the Best New Singer Award

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:43.700
in the Fantasia Music Festival?!

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:53.260
Is it really that amazing of an award?

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:56.160
It's not just amazing.

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:58.730
It's the only international music festival

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:02.760
for which Japan is in association
with America's AAS Broadcasting.

00:03:02.830 --> 00:03:03.860
Wow.

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:07.100
In addition, what's unique
about this festival is that

00:03:07.130 --> 00:03:09.360
the audience gets to vote
alongside the judges.

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:12.360
That's why your performance
on that day is important

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:14.960
in order to get a lot of votes
from the audience.

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:17.360
We have to improve your
condition from now on.

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:19.800
I can't really grasp it all quite yet.

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:24.760
But what I'm about to tell
you will really get you motivated!

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:27.260
You see, the winner of
the Best New Singer Award

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:28.830
will be invited to America.

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:29.930
What?!

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:31.230
America?

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:36.460
America... I'll get to see Eichi.

00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:39.760
You have to win! Right?

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:47.730
It's a really big music festival.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:54.800
Hey! You're so cute!

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:57.160
You're waiting for an email
from Eichi, aren't you?

00:03:57.260 --> 00:04:00.060
N-No! That's not it.

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:02.600
It's just that if I hold my cell phone,

00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:06.300
I feel like I'm connected to Eichi,
and it calms me down.

00:04:06.530 --> 00:04:08.730
Aww, I'm jealous!

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:10.200
Stop it, Ms. Oshige!

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:12.830
Full Moon, we'll start the explanation!

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:15.760
Oh, okay! Ms. Oshige,
please hold these for me.

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:16.600
Okay.

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:22.900
She's been so happy since
she got the email from Eichi.

00:04:23.130 --> 00:04:26.060
Yes. On top of that, there's the news
of the new treatment method,

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:27.560
and the Best New Singer Award
nomination.

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:31.730
I'm sure that if she got
about 100 emails from Eichi,

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:33.560
her illness would be cured.

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:38.560
Dr. Wakaoji!

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:39.760
Hi.

00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:43.560
Ms. Oshige... Umm...
Did I get any emails?

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:44.800
No.

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:46.500
I see.

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:51.430
Hey, they say no news is good news.

00:04:52.260 --> 00:04:58.330
That's okay! Because I'm really happy
with that one email from Eichi.

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:01.060
Hey...

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:06.430
Don't you think we should tell her
that the email was fake after all?

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:07.330
No!

00:06:08.030 --> 00:06:09.760
She's so happy!

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:12.230
It's an important time with
the Best New Singer Award.

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:14.100
To tell her that now...

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:18.760
But isn't it crueler to make her
happy with lies?

00:06:19.530 --> 00:06:20.500
Takuto!

00:06:25.430 --> 00:06:27.430
Full Moon, please.

00:06:27.660 --> 00:06:28.460
Okay.

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:57.300
She needs an email from Eichi.

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:07.760
DEAR MITSUKI
I'M ALWAYS LISTENING
TO YOUR SONGS.
GOOD LUCK WITH
THE BEST
NEW SINGER AWARD.
—EICHI

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:12.160
SEND

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:23.200
Hey, hey! Takuto!

00:07:23.660 --> 00:07:26.560
Do you want to see
the new email from Eichi?

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:28.060
Not really.

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:31.230
Don't say that!
See, see! Look!

00:07:31.330 --> 00:07:33.730
It's kind of short and curt, but...

00:07:35.060 --> 00:07:37.800
He's probably just busy, right?

00:07:38.030 --> 00:07:39.560
I don't know.

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:43.060
<i>Yeah, because I wrote it! Darn it!</i>

00:07:43.700 --> 00:07:49.160
But even though it's short,
I can feel that he's thinking about me.

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:51.700
I understand.

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:54.500
I feel like his true feelings are in
this short email

00:07:54.530 --> 00:07:59.130
more than in the long one that I got first.

00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:01.130
I wonder why.

00:08:04.930 --> 00:08:06.760
Hello? Is this Meroko?

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:11.160
Tomorrow, I'm going to stay at home.
So please stay with her.

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:13.330
Yeah, see ya.

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:28.430
Hey! Oshige!

00:08:29.230 --> 00:08:30.800
Oh, Department Manager.

00:08:31.730 --> 00:08:32.530
Who's this?

00:08:33.330 --> 00:08:35.230
I'm going to make my debut soon.

00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:38.300
I'm Yuma Shimazu.
I'm looking forward to working with you.

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:41.900
I guess you could say
she's Full Moon's junior.

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:43.800
I've always admired you.

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:47.630
Full Moon, I look forward to
working with you.

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:49.600
I look forward to working with you too.

00:08:50.060 --> 00:08:51.430
Thank you.

00:08:51.930 --> 00:08:54.130
Wow, what a cute plush toy.

00:08:54.900 --> 00:08:56.430
May I see it?

00:08:57.560 --> 00:08:58.830
Y-Yeah, here.

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:00.260
Wow.

00:09:03.030 --> 00:09:05.130
It's about time for the meeting to start.

00:09:05.160 --> 00:09:06.960
Department Manager, I'll see you later.

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:07.700
Yeah.

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:11.630
<i>Don't leave me here!</i>

00:09:31.100 --> 00:09:33.130
<i>An email? Could it be Eichi?</i>

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:38.160
Jeez...

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:40.830
It's not easy being in the plush toy form.

00:09:45.330 --> 00:09:46.760
Ow! What the...

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:48.300
Meroko! I'm so glad I found you!

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:51.460
I have to go to Narita Airport
right away!

00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:55.530
I got an email from Eichi!
He's coming to Japan today!

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:56.130
What?

00:09:56.600 --> 00:10:00.660
So please tell Takuto to come
to Narita Airport!

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:01.760
W-Wait!

00:10:01.860 --> 00:10:03.600
I'll be back before the show!

00:10:25.430 --> 00:10:28.100
That Mitsuki...
I wonder where she went.

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:33.860
This is Oshige.

00:10:35.660 --> 00:10:37.930
Oh, Mitsuki? Hey, where are you?

00:10:38.560 --> 00:10:39.200
What?

00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:41.230
What?! Eiichi is here?!

00:10:41.830 --> 00:10:44.560
Yes, I'll definitely return before the show.

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:46.900
So please let me go to Narita Airport.

00:10:48.560 --> 00:10:49.460
<i>I understand.</i>

00:10:50.260 --> 00:10:51.800
<i>I'll be waiting for you, Mitsuki.</i>

00:10:52.300 --> 00:10:53.730
<i>Thank you, Ms. Oshige!</i>

00:10:56.600 --> 00:10:57.600
All right!

00:10:58.200 --> 00:10:59.200
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:02.900
I don't know! Anyway, she told me
to tell you to go to Narita.

00:11:03.130 --> 00:11:04.430
<i>I understand. I'll go at once.</i>

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:10.660
Yay, were you surprised?

00:11:10.930 --> 00:11:12.660
Mero, how are you?

00:11:13.660 --> 00:11:14.600
Izumi...

00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:16.060
Hi!

00:11:17.260 --> 00:11:19.400
I can't believe
you were surprised by that.

00:11:19.430 --> 00:11:20.700
Maybe you're getting old.

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:25.330
What do you want?
I'm busy now. Bye.

00:11:27.100 --> 00:11:30.630
It looks like Mitsuki fell
for the email I sent.

00:11:31.260 --> 00:11:33.630
Mitsuki is really innocent and cute.

00:11:33.760 --> 00:11:34.730
What did you say?!

00:11:35.560 --> 00:11:36.600
About the email?

00:11:36.930 --> 00:11:42.100
You told me to quit it,
but Takuto's doing it himself.

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:45.460
That's why I started emailing again.

00:11:45.960 --> 00:11:47.800
Takuto sent...an email?

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:50.860
So I collaborated and wrote,

00:11:50.900 --> 00:11:54.460
"Today I'm returning to Narita.
I'd like you to pick me up."

00:11:55.030 --> 00:11:55.960
How could you?!

00:11:56.560 --> 00:11:57.730
What's this?

00:11:57.760 --> 00:12:01.930
Mero, aren't you happy that Mitsuki's
feelings are directed at Eichi?

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:04.100
I want you to thank me.

00:12:06.760 --> 00:12:09.960
We'll start rehearsal.
Please start, Ms. Komaki.

00:12:10.300 --> 00:12:12.030
Our special guest today is the winner

00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:15.960
of last year's Best New Singer Award,
The Scanty.

00:12:25.960 --> 00:12:30.200
<i>I want to be a Rock n' Roll Princess!</i>

00:12:30.230 --> 00:12:33.430
<i>And dance with the rock spirit!</i>

00:12:34.260 --> 00:12:38.160
<i>My heart throbs... Oh Rock Star!</i>

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:42.430
<i>Crying out a scream of love!</i>

00:12:45.400 --> 00:12:46.260
Meroko!

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:48.230
Takuto!

00:12:48.660 --> 00:12:50.160
What in the world happened?

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:51.400
I'd like to ask you!

00:12:51.430 --> 00:12:54.100
What's this about you sending
an email to Mitsuki?!

00:12:54.130 --> 00:12:55.260
Th-That was...

00:12:55.300 --> 00:12:59.360
Izumi jumped on the bandwagon and
sent an email again because you did!

00:12:59.500 --> 00:13:00.300
What?!

00:13:00.730 --> 00:13:02.000
That Izumi...

00:13:03.630 --> 00:13:04.760
Hey, Takuto.

00:13:05.030 --> 00:13:09.200
I know what Izumi did was wrong,
but you sent a fake email too, right?

00:13:11.030 --> 00:13:13.860
If it's false hope,
then we shouldn't make her wait!

00:13:14.460 --> 00:13:17.130
That will hurt her unnecessarily.

00:13:19.230 --> 00:13:23.360
For whatever reason you did it,
it's still the same as what Izumi did.

00:13:24.460 --> 00:13:25.330
Sorry.

00:13:26.300 --> 00:13:27.530
Oh, c'mon!

00:13:27.560 --> 00:13:29.400
I have a load of things
I want to say to you!

00:13:29.860 --> 00:13:31.900
But before that,
we have to go get Mitsuki!

00:13:40.700 --> 00:13:43.600
<i>Thank you, The Scanty!</i>

00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:49.760
FULL MOON
<i>I want to scream in</i>
<i>the winter sky that...</i>

00:13:50.160 --> 00:13:52.060
<i>I want to see you right now!</i>

00:13:52.060 --> 00:13:58.830
FULL MOON
<i>I want to see you right now!</i>

00:14:02.300 --> 00:14:07.560
Good work. Please tell Mitsuki the plan
and where she'll need to stand.

00:14:08.960 --> 00:14:10.930
And that's all for
the Best New Singer Award!

00:14:11.600 --> 00:14:14.360
It's difficult being a manager, isn't it?

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:15.500
Isn't it?

00:14:15.530 --> 00:14:17.860
Well, that doesn't usually happen.

00:14:36.960 --> 00:14:38.630
Takuto, Meroko...

00:14:39.760 --> 00:14:41.900
Hey, hurry up and change me
back into Mitsuki.

00:14:42.160 --> 00:14:44.460
I can't meet Eichi like this.

00:14:45.800 --> 00:14:46.760
Sorry!

00:14:47.000 --> 00:14:47.700
What?

00:14:50.400 --> 00:14:51.260
I'm sorry.

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:53.760
I sent that short email.

00:14:55.030 --> 00:14:56.700
The first email and...

00:14:57.860 --> 00:15:00.360
the one that says he's coming home
were from Izumi.

00:15:00.630 --> 00:15:01.260
What?

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:04.360
None of the emails were from Eichi.

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:06.300
And it's a lie that he's coming home.

00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:10.800
The emails weren't real? So Eichi is...

00:15:11.430 --> 00:15:13.430
We still don't know where he is.

00:15:13.730 --> 00:15:14.630
No way!

00:15:16.100 --> 00:15:18.800
I thought I was going to see Eichi soon.

00:15:19.530 --> 00:15:20.860
H-Hey, Mitsuki...

00:15:34.230 --> 00:15:38.300
HEY MITSUKI,
SORRY FOR THE SHORT NOTICE,
BUT I'M GOING TO JAPAN TODAY.
MY FLIGHT LANDS AT 15:45,
SO WOULD YOU COME GET ME
AT THE AIRPORT?
I'M LOOKING FORWARD TO
SEEING YOU AT THE AIRPORT.
—EICHI

00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:44.360
Sorry! By sending the thoughtless email,
I've made you suffer.

00:15:44.960 --> 00:15:46.030
I'm really sorry!

00:15:53.060 --> 00:15:53.960
Mitsuki...

00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:54.660
It's okay.

00:15:55.860 --> 00:16:00.760
It's okay. After all,
you did it for me, right, Takuto?

00:16:03.230 --> 00:16:06.130
I'm going to the music festival
to sing on stage.

00:16:06.330 --> 00:16:09.460
And I'm going to win
the Best New Singer Award for Eichi.

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:11.400
For Eichi? But you...

00:16:11.500 --> 00:16:15.260
If we don't know where Eichi is,
I'll go search for him!

00:16:15.800 --> 00:16:20.060
Until I met you two,
I had given up hope on everything.

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:22.560
But that's no good...

00:16:23.130 --> 00:16:26.400
If I want to see Eichi again,
I have to go to America.

00:16:27.260 --> 00:16:29.060
So I'm going to win
the Best New Singer Award!

00:16:31.100 --> 00:16:33.000
You've gotten so strong, Mitsuki.

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:40.900
WOULD YOU LIKE TO DELETE
THIS EMAIL?
YES/NO

00:16:50.260 --> 00:16:51.200
Ms. Oshige!

00:16:52.160 --> 00:16:54.330
Dr. Wakaoji. Did you find her?

00:16:55.100 --> 00:16:57.730
I returned to the waiting room,
but there was no evidence of her.

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:00.660
It's all my fault.

00:17:01.800 --> 00:17:03.830
That doesn't matter now.

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:05.900
Let's search for her together
one more time.

00:17:07.400 --> 00:17:09.360
<i>That was the third nominee</i>
<i>for Best New Singer,</i>

00:17:09.400 --> 00:17:10.900
<i>The Drill Boys.</i>

00:17:11.500 --> 00:17:13.100
Oh no! She's on!

00:17:13.230 --> 00:17:15.330
<i>And now, the final nominees.</i>

00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:16.860
It's all over!

00:17:17.460 --> 00:17:19.700
<i>We can trust that</i>
<i>this wonderful performance</i>

00:17:19.730 --> 00:17:22.230
<i>will sparkle like the moon</i>
<i>in the evening sky.</i>

00:17:23.030 --> 00:17:24.260
<i>Full Moon!</i>

00:17:32.700 --> 00:17:36.200
<i>How long has it been</i>

00:17:36.460 --> 00:17:40.930
<i>since I fell in love with you?</i>

00:17:41.730 --> 00:17:50.030
<i>My feelings keep getting stronger.</i>

00:17:50.660 --> 00:17:59.100
<i>They're silent like the snow,</i>

00:17:59.800 --> 00:18:09.900
<i>but they keep building up.</i>

00:18:11.500 --> 00:18:19.030
<i>Hold me tight, if loving someone</i>

00:18:20.130 --> 00:18:26.030
<i>was going to feel like this</i>

00:18:26.060 --> 00:18:29.460
<i>I wish I never found out about love.</i>

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:32.130
<i>I love you.</i>

00:18:32.530 --> 00:18:36.960
<i>My tears won't stop.</i>

00:18:37.830 --> 00:18:41.300
<i>If this is how it's going to be,</i>

00:18:41.330 --> 00:18:51.330
<i>I wish I had never met you.</i>

00:18:52.460 --> 00:18:59.960
<i>If the snow falls forever...</i>

00:19:00.560 --> 00:19:10.760
<i>Will I be able to let go of</i>
<i>these thoughts of you?</i>

00:19:12.100 --> 00:19:14.800
<i>Hold me tight,</i>

00:19:14.960 --> 00:19:20.160
<i>if this is how it feels</i>

00:19:20.760 --> 00:19:26.430
<i>to fall in love with someone</i>

00:19:26.500 --> 00:19:29.760
<i>I wish I never knew.</i>

00:19:29.960 --> 00:19:37.900
<i>I love you,</i>
<i>the feeling of love fills my heart.</i>

00:19:37.960 --> 00:19:42.760
<i>I want to scream in the winter sky that</i>

00:19:43.200 --> 00:19:51.830
<i>I want to see you right now.</i>

00:20:06.930 --> 00:20:08.530
That was amazing, Mitsuki!

00:20:08.730 --> 00:20:10.300
Mitsuki, you did very well!

00:20:10.400 --> 00:20:13.160
Wow! She did it! That was awesome.

00:20:13.330 --> 00:20:14.830
Way to go, Mitsuki.

00:20:15.330 --> 00:20:18.200
<i>Eichi, are you listening to my song...</i>

00:20:20.130 --> 00:20:22.760
<i>from somewhere?</i>

00:20:27.100 --> 00:20:29.430
Congratulations to winner
of the Best New Singer Award!

00:20:29.460 --> 00:20:31.600
- Yay!
- Thank you!

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:35.860
I'm drinking today.

00:20:35.930 --> 00:20:40.330
I can't believe you didn't return until just
before your performance, you rascal!

00:20:40.500 --> 00:20:42.760
I'm sorry, Ms. Oshige. Sorry.

00:20:42.900 --> 00:20:44.760
Well, well, let's let it go.

00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:48.500
Yeah! You won Best New Singer
with a huge lead!

00:20:48.760 --> 00:20:51.600
Yeah, you were number one with both
the audience votes

00:20:51.630 --> 00:20:53.260
and with the judge's votes.

00:20:53.300 --> 00:20:56.660
I know, I'm not that much of
a stick in the mud.

00:20:59.600 --> 00:21:01.060
This is Mitsuki.

00:21:03.000 --> 00:21:04.030
Ms. Kazumi?

00:21:05.300 --> 00:21:06.230
What?!

00:21:06.700 --> 00:21:08.100
Is this really true?

00:21:08.430 --> 00:21:11.800
Yes... yes...
Thank you very much!

00:21:12.360 --> 00:21:14.260
What's going on, Mitsuki?

00:21:14.530 --> 00:21:18.730
Eichi... She said she got
a lead on Eichi!

00:21:19.360 --> 00:21:21.330
- What?
- Really, Mitsuki?

00:21:21.400 --> 00:21:23.260
Yes! That was Ms. Kazumi!

00:21:24.200 --> 00:21:25.260
No way!

00:21:27.100 --> 00:21:28.360
<i>This time...</i>

00:21:30.030 --> 00:21:33.760
<i>This time, for sure,</i>
<i>we'll find Eichi!</i>

00:23:06.560 --> 00:23:07.630
Takuto!

00:23:07.660 --> 00:23:09.600
W-What's with you all of a sudden?!

00:23:09.660 --> 00:23:11.830
You're so mean!
You know what I'm going to say!

00:23:12.030 --> 00:23:13.960
Just give me some breathing room!

00:23:14.100 --> 00:23:16.660
Gosh, do you want me to
spell it out for you?

00:23:16.700 --> 00:23:19.300
Today is the romantic Christmas!

00:23:19.330 --> 00:23:22.460
It's as though the whole town
is celebrating our love!

00:23:22.660 --> 00:23:23.760
What?! He's gone?!

00:23:23.830 --> 00:23:25.430
Wait up!

00:23:26.260 --> 00:23:30.330
Next time on Full Moon:
"A Present from Full Moon"

00:23:30.630 --> 00:23:32.030
- Look forward to it!
- Look forward to it!
